2. 
cwnd = 1. After a timeout the sender doesn't trust the network at all, so it starts over
with slow start, which climbs quickly back to 
ssthresh (the new, lower boundary)
and then goes gently.
Slow increase plus fast decrease is called AIMD. It is used because it is stable and fair. If
two senders share a link and one has more, the cuts hurt the bigger one more (halving
takes more away) while both gain the same +1 per RTT, so over time they converge to
equal shares.
